{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm","id":929022,"title":"Disguising others charm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-09T19:44:43-07:00","id":929022,"title":"Disguising others charm","content":"Does Essence 2 sound appropriate for a Charm that allows one to apply Flawless Impenetrable Disguise to others?<br /> <br /> And then an Essence 3 Charm (that requires both the above and Perfect Mirror), allows you to apply Perfect Mirror to others?<br /> <br /> Does there need to be a limit on how many disguises you can have going on others at a time? Or maybe an essence commitment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T20:25:43-07:00","id":929030,"title":"","content":"I think you shouldn't be able to provide others with more than (Essence) disguises, AND that it should require the commitment of the motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:03:30-07:00","id":929077,"title":"","content":"You can just disguise other people with Disguise of the New Face. You always could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:37:26-07:00","id":929081,"title":"","content":"Ah, didn't think to look in sorcery. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T23:43:51-07:00","id":929083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929077#post929077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just disguise other people with Disguise of the New Face. You always could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am guessing this thread is about 3e, which has no such effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11878-realbrickwall","name":"realbrickwall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T00:09:46-07:00","id":929091,"title":"","content":"Or never mind, back to my original question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T04:09:23-07:00","id":929171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>realbrickwall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929083#post929083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am guessing this thread is about 3e, which has no such effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a spell in 1e. It was a spell in 2e. There's no reason to assume it won't or can't exist in the new-but-inspired-by-the-best-of-1e paradigm of Ex3. In fact, folks have already made attempts at homebrewing their own version.<br /> <br /> It's not like the so-called &quot;factions&quot; of the Silver Pact in 2e, or the idea that basically everything in the setting should be antagonistic toward the Sidereals (<i>especially</i> the Sidereals themselves!), where the devs explicitly called it out as bullshit - it's a cool, evocative sorcery spell that doesn't render worthless actual investment in actual disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-10-2016, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T05:17:55-07:00","id":929201,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd allow a Perfect Mirror-alike on others. Disguising others (even multiple people with a single activation), though, that I can see.<br /> <br /> I'd expect mote commitments for each individual person, but also bonuses if they remain in your immediate vicinity. This would represent your character helping the beneficiaries stay in character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929171#post929171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a spell in 1e. It was a spell in 2e. There's no reason to assume it won't or can't exist in the new-but-inspired-by-the-best-of-1e paradigm of Ex3. In fact, folks have already made attempts at homebrewing their own version.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? Glamourweaver asked for help with balancing/designing a Charm. Saying &quot;well, there'll <i>eventually</i> be a spell for that&quot; doesn't really help with that. For one, sorcery requires a heavier investment, concept-wise, than a Larceny Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T05:30:27-07:00","id":929202,"title":"","content":"Actually, not only are they comparable, but if the Larceny Charm requires Perfect Mirror as a prereq, DotNF is the cheaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T06:12:29-07:00","id":929210,"title":"","content":"I would just make them essence commitment and repurchases on the charms at different essence to affect others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T09:25:55-07:00","id":929251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929171#post929171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a spell in 1e. It was a spell in 2e. There's no reason to assume it won't or can't exist in the new-but-inspired-by-the-best-of-1e paradigm of Ex3. In fact, folks have already made attempts at homebrewing their own version.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a designer, I'm not really a fan of spells that do something in a way that just totally blows the Ability that normally does the thing out of the water. Stuff like Disguise of the New Face, the Eye and the Mouth, Peacock Shadow Eyes, etc. <br /> <br /> That's not to say Disguise of the New Face can't or won't show up in Ex3, but it shouldn't invalidate cool Larceny Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T10:05:34-07:00","id":929260,"title":"","content":"Well, Solar Larceny Charms can make you immune to mundane and supernatural detection, maybe Disguise of the New Face allows a differing dice pool and just makes it convincing to mundane senses but doesn't prevent supernatural ones from detecting it? Or maybe it just augments it?<br /> <br /> I was looking at a fan conversion of disguise of the new face, one of shadow peacock eyes and of Of Dreams and Nightmares, and it occurred to me how the last of those three is way more flavorful, even if I feel like hypnotism or illusory disguises seem apropos for sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T10:12:30-07:00","id":929265,"title":"","content":"Peacock Shadow Eyes is an interesting one, given how social influence and associated Charms were intended to move away from mind control.<br /> <br /> You get the question of how difficult sorcerous mind control should be that it's not the default solution, while also being circumstantially easier than trying to convince somebody to do something more directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T11:23:39-07:00","id":929286,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar527_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"527\" data-vbnamecard=\"527\">Robert Vance</a>: Like I was saying, DotNF doesn't invalidate Larceny - in part, because it's still a Larceny roll to make the disguise (unless you're a Sidereal), and in part, because it's still penetrable in a way that Flawless Impenetrable Disguise is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:40:36-07:00","id":929476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929286#post929286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: Like I was saying, DotNF doesn't invalidate Larceny - in part, because it's still a Larceny roll to make the disguise (unless you're a Sidereal), and in part, because it's still penetrable in a way that Flawless Impenetrable Disguise is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the positive of it being a Spell though? What does it thematically bring to the table there rather than as a Larceny Charm?<br /> <br /> Is it just so Mortal Sorcerers can access it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:41:53-07:00","id":929478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929476#post929476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the positive of it being a Spell though? What does it thematically bring to the table there rather than as a Larceny Charm?<br /> <br /> Is it just so Mortal Sorcerers can access it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or any other kind of Exalt? It probably wouldn't function the same way as a Solar Larceny Charm, and definitely wouldn't be as good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:41:55-07:00","id":929479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929251#post929251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a designer, I'm not really a fan of spells that do something in a way that just totally blows the Ability that normally does the thing out of the water. Stuff like Disguise of the New Face, the Eye and the Mouth, Peacock Shadow Eyes, etc. <br /> <br /> That's not to say Disguise of the New Face can't or won't show up in Ex3, but it shouldn't invalidate cool Larceny Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can hear the people who want to build Solar soak-monsters out of Resistance Charms grumbling from here...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:52:33-07:00","id":929486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929478#post929478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or any other kind of Exalt? It probably wouldn't function the same way as a Solar Larceny Charm, and definitely wouldn't be as good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still feels to me like an area that should be well covered by native Charms in different thematic ways rather than just using Sorcery as some sort of catchall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:57:37-07:00","id":929487,"title":"","content":"Disguise of a New Face changes your anima/caste mark. Sidereal NPCs use it to pass at other types of Exalts, if they don't have that one SMA. Might not be needed in Ex3, since Sidereals can pass at Exigents instead of Dragonblooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:59:37-07:00","id":929488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929487#post929487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disguise of a New Face changes your anima/caste mark. Sidereal NPCs use it to pass at other types of Exalts, if they don't have that one SMA. Might not be needed in Ex3, since Sidereals can pass at Exigents instead of Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they just have native disguise charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T19:01:01-07:00","id":929489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929488#post929488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they just have native disguise charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope Sidereals do have Native Disguise charms in Ex3! Or Resplendent Destinies covered different anima effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T01:03:22-07:00","id":929611,"title":"","content":"Horned to Hornless, Hornless to Horned<br /> <br /> Cost: 6m Mins: Larceny 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keyword: None<br /> Duration: Until the sapient subject sleeps, or indefinite for non-sapient subject<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flawless Impenetrable Disguise<br /> <br /> The Solar may apply the effects of Flawless Impenetrable Disguise to willing subjects, or docile/trained non-sapient subjects (making one animal look entirely different, disguising its color, adding or hiding horns, giving it a thick coat, scales, etc). The Solar must commit the 6 motes for the duration of the disguise's effect, and they may only have as many active disguises beyond their own equal to their Essence. A disguise on a non-sapient animal will last indefinitely, but will collapse once someone sees through the disguise or the Solar uncommites the motes. The animal's noises, stance, etc are covered by the illusion, but the Charm cannot compel an animal's behavior. A cow disguised as a large ferocious lion may start grazing when it is hungry, threatening the disguise to onlookers.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be repurchased an unlimited number of times starting at Essence 3. Each repurchase allows for [Essence] more disguises to be maintained at a time.<br /> <br /> The subjects of a Solar Master of Disguise are not capable of the true mastery of the art of impersonation she is capable of. The upgrade effects of Perfect Mirror do not apply to disguises upon others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:42:58-07:00","id":929903,"title":"","content":"Any comments on that charm write-up or should I make a new PEACH thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:33:27-07:00","id":1384230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=929611#post929611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horned to Hornless, Hornless to Horned<br /> <br /> Cost: 6m Mins: Larceny 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keyword: None<br /> Duration: Until the sapient subject sleeps, or indefinite for non-sapient subject<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flawless Impenetrable Disguise<br /> <br /> The Solar may apply the effects of Flawless Impenetrable Disguise to willing subjects, or docile/trained non-sapient subjects (making one animal look entirely different, disguising its color, adding or hiding horns, giving it a thick coat, scales, etc). The Solar must commit the 6 motes for the duration of the disguise's effect, and they may only have as many active disguises beyond their own equal to their Essence. A disguise on a non-sapient animal will last indefinitely, but will collapse once someone sees through the disguise or the Solar uncommites the motes. The animal's noises, stance, etc are covered by the illusion, but the Charm cannot compel an animal's behavior. A cow disguised as a large ferocious lion may start grazing when it is hungry, threatening the disguise to onlookers.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be repurchased an unlimited number of times starting at Essence 3. Each repurchase allows for [Essence] more disguises to be maintained at a time.<br /> <br /> The subjects of a Solar Master of Disguise are not capable of the true mastery of the art of impersonation she is capable of. The upgrade effects of Perfect Mirror do not apply to disguises upon others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi 4 years ago me! Someone liked a comment on this thread to summon me back. I have absolutely no idea why I thought it was so important to regulate the number of disguises a Solar could commit motes to make. Drop all references to a limit on number of disguises, and the repurchase option. Committing the motes is check enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:31:55-07:00","id":1384241,"title":"","content":"Given Vance's comment on Peacock Shadow Eyes, it's interesting to compare the current version to the 2e version.<br /> <br /> 2e Peacock Shadow Eyes indeed totally ignored social Abilities and replaced them with a Wits+Occult roll; the 3e version still requires actual social skills to make good use of the spell, although the spell certainly makes things easier in several ways.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that if we see Disguise of the New Face return at all, the sorcerer will need some actual Larceny skills to use the spell effectively. I'm having trouble thinking of an interesting mechanic for that effect, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T22:18:26-07:00","id":1384357,"title":"","content":"Guardian Shadow Approach similar to \u200bGuardian Fog Approach<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Larceny 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise<br /> Through quick action, the Solar may obscure someone<br /> with her own efforts to remain hidden. The Solar must<br /> be touching the one she wishes to hide, and must herself<br /> attempt a Disguise action at the same time. The Solar works<br /> to obscure her charge, covering him with her body, shrouding<br /> him with her cloak, or guiding him into a cleverly concealed<br /> disguise. Add half the Solar\u2019s successes (rounded up)<br /> and any stunt bonuses on this action as dice to her charge\u2019s<br /> own Larceny roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:27:06-07:00","id":1385444,"title":"","content":"Thinking on this, I feel like there should either be a general \u201cassist other\u201d ability that can be put into play here or set of more specific \u201cdisguise other,\u201d \u201chide other,\u201d and so on abilities.<br /> <br /> This would require reworking a few charms, but I really don\u2019t think that pulling someone behind you and hiding them under your cloak, making them up as someone else, or clapping your hand over their mouth before they say something stupid should require a Charm to even attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T14:51:32-07:00","id":1385462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=1385444#post1385444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on this, I feel like there should either be a general \u201cassist other\u201d ability that can be put into play here or set of more specific \u201cdisguise other,\u201d \u201chide other,\u201d and so on abilities.<br /> <br /> This would require reworking a few charms, but I really don\u2019t think that pulling someone behind you and hiding them under your cloak, making them up as someone else, or clapping your hand over their mouth before they say something stupid should require a Charm to even attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, just as you don\u2019t need Flawless Impenetrable Disguise to try and disguise yourself. But how putting a supernaturally flawless disguise on someone else is another matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T02:12:01-07:00","id":1385563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=1385444#post1385444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on this, I feel like there should either be a general \u201cassist other\u201d ability that can be put into play here or set of more specific \u201cdisguise other,\u201d \u201chide other,\u201d and so on abilities.<br /> <br /> This would require reworking a few charms, but I really don\u2019t think that pulling someone behind you and hiding them under your cloak, making them up as someone else, or clapping your hand over their mouth before they say something stupid should require a Charm to even attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Stunt fodder. You are describing Stunts.<br /> <br /> More generally, I like Guardian Fog Approach because not being discovered is essential to Stealth.<br /> I like Tiger Warrior Training Technique because it applies to your subordinates.<br /> <br /> I don't sit comfortably with Solar Charms that are about cooperation and teamwork. It's not really their design space.<br /> <br /> Being personally Excellent, including leading with excellence? Yes.<br /> Making others Excellent? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T11:19:47-07:00","id":1385626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929022-disguising-others-charm?p=1385563#post1385563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't sit comfortably with Solar Charms that are about cooperation and teamwork. It's not really their design space.<br /> <br /> Being personally Excellent, including leading with excellence? Yes.<br /> Making others Excellent? No.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is about YOU being really good at applying disguises.<br /> <br /> I do also think Solar leadership can allow for working your excellence through others effects. We\u2019ve seen that done with Presence (\u201cI speak in the name of [Solar]!\u201d). I also think there\u2019s room in Solar themes to... let\u2019s say... work your Medicine Charms through the rest of the triage team who have consecrated their instruments in your name - the big thing with Solar Charms to this effect, unlike the DB Charms, is that they\u2019re about extending your glory through your subordinates. So while DBs tend to do new cool things through pooled efforts of DB peers - Solars are more likely just applying their usual Charms through (probably mortal) subordinates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}